{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Algebra.InfiniteSum.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Vol_Borromean_eq_eight_Catalan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Vol_Borromean_eq_eight_Catalan","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L153-L157","doc":"**Borromean volume in terms of Catalan constant.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.catalan_constant_eq_cl_2_pi_over_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.catalan_constant_eq_cl_2_pi_over_2","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L142-L151","doc":"**Borromean = 8 · Catalan_constant equality.** The standard\nidentification: `G = Cl_2(π/2)` (NOT `Cl_2(π/2)`), so\n`Catalan_constant = Cl_2(π/2) = G ≈ 0.91596`. The Borromean\nrings hyperbolic volume `8G = 8·Cl_2(π/2)` decomposes via\n2 ideal regular octahedra, each of which is 4 ideal tetrahedra\nof shape parameter `i = e^{iπ/2}` contributing\n`Cl_2(π/2) = G` per tetrahedron. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Vol_Borromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Vol_Borromean","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L132-L140","doc":"**Borromean rings hyperbolic volume carrier.** By the\n2-octahedron decomposition, each ideal regular octahedron\ndecomposes into 4 ideal tetrahedra of shape parameter\n`i = e^{iπ/2}`, each contributing `Cl_2(π/2) = G` (Catalan).\nPer octahedron = `4G = 4·Cl_2(π/2)`; total Borromean\nvolume = `8G = 8·Cl_2(π/2)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Vol_figure_8","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Vol_figure_8","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L123-L130","doc":"**Figure-8 hyperbolic volume carrier.** By the Thurston\n2-tetrahedra triangulation [`thurston1978`], the figure-8 knot\ncomplement decomposes into 2 ideal regular tetrahedra of shape\nparameter `e^{iπ/3}`, each contributing `Cl_2(π/3)`.\nTherefore `Vol(4_1) = 2 · Cl_2(π/3)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Catalan_constant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Catalan_constant","kind":"def","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L114-L121","doc":"**Catalan constant carrier:** `G = Cl_2(π/2)`. The numerical\nvalue `G ≈ 0.91596...` is the imaginary part of the\ndilogarithm at `i = e^{iπ/2}` and gives the per-octahedron\ncontribution to the Borromean rings hyperbolic volume\n`Vol(B_3) = 8G`\n([`binding-scale-catalan`](../braids-and-knots/binding-scale-catalan.md)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2_two_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2_two_pi","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L101-L112","doc":"**Boundary lemma:** `Cl_2(2π) = 0` (the right endpoint of the\nfundamental domain). Each term is `sin(2(k+1)π) = 0`. This is the\n`Cl_2_two_pi` promised in the file docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2_pi","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L88-L99","doc":"**Boundary lemma:** `Cl_2(π) = 0`. Each term is\n`sin((k+1)π) = 0` (`sin` at an integer multiple of `π`). Filled in\nper the docstring's \"unconditional boundary lemmas\"; needs no\nFourier infrastructure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2_zero","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L83-L86","doc":"**Boundary lemma:** `Cl_2(0) = 0`. Each term is `sin(0) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.Cl_2","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller.lean#L69-L81","doc":"The **Clausen function** `Cl_2 : ℝ → ℝ` defined by the Fourier\nseries\n\n  Cl_2(θ) := Σ_{k≥1} sin(k θ) / k²\n\nvia Mathlib's `tsum`. The series converges absolutely and\nuniformly on all of `ℝ` (since `|sin(k θ) / k²| ≤ 1 / k²`),\nThe `tsum` is well-defined and continuous. Outside the\nstandard fundamental domain `[0, 2π]` the function extends\nby periodicity (`Cl_2(θ + 2π) = Cl_2(θ)`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}